{
  "abstract": "We study composite automorphism group actions on $(K_5,I_5)$-free graphs near the lower-bound frontier $43\\le R(5,5)\\le46$, without assuming regularity or strong regularity. First, we prove an elementary minimal-subgroup reduction showing that every finite group of order $2^a\\cdot3$ with $a\\ge2$ contains one of the five groups of order $12$ ($A_4$, $D_6\\cong S_3\\times C_2$, $C_{12}$, $C_6\\times C_2$, or $\\operatorname{Dic}_3$) or the binary tetrahedral group $\\operatorname{SL}(2,3)$ of order $24$. Combining the published $A_4$ exclusion with exhaustive orbit-type classification ($573{,}081$ canonical faithful tuples and $27{,}011$ strict survivors), row-canonical symmetry breaking, and independently verified reverse unit propagation (RUP) refutations across all $6{,}184$ strict minimal faithful roots at orders $42\\le N\\le45$ ($5{,}173$ for $D_6$, $155$ for $C_{12}$, $155$ for $\\operatorname{Dic}_3$, $610$ for $C_6\\times C_2$, and $91$ for $\\operatorname{SL}(2,3)$, totaling $305{,}773{,}252$ RUP clauses), we prove that no group of order $2^a\\cdot3$ ($a\\ge2$) acts faithfully on any $(K_5,I_5)$-free graph of order $42\\le N\\le45$. This does not improve $43\\le R(5,5)\\le46$; pure $2$-groups ($|H|=2^a$), order-$3$ ($C_3$) and order-$6$ ($C_6,S_3$) actions, non-conference $5$-actions at order $45$, and lower orders $N\\le41$ (specifically $N=41$ for $D_6,C_{12},\\operatorname{Dic}_3,C_6\\times C_2$) remain open. Separately, we establish the sharp global maximum $N_{\\max}(\\operatorname{SL}(2,3))=40$ via `SL23_40` ($|\\operatorname{Aut}|=192$, degrees $20^{24}21^{16}$) and construct a non-isomorphic order-$40$ realization `D6_40` ($|\\operatorname{Aut}|=24$, degrees $17^{12}18^{16}19^{12}$), both RUP-certified non-$(3,3,5)$-splittable in both orientations.",
